  label the lambda on line 18 is freed at the end of its block
  help copy the data with `.copy(to: alloc)` into an allocator that lives long enough
BYN3002 23:16 the lambda on line 23 does not live as long as `last`, which borrows it
  label the lambda on line 23 is freed at the end of its block
  help copy the data with `.copy(to: alloc)` into an allocator that lives long enough
BYN3003 29:16 cannot return a borrow of the lambda on line 29, which is freed when `main$lambda7` returns
  help let the caller pass the buffer or allocator in, and borrow or allocate from that
